One request, two providers, one Reply type.

  openai        stop=tool_calls tool=query_warehouse   147/40   tokens
  block-shaped  stop=tool_calls tool=query_warehouse    41/17   tokens

What the adapter had to translate to get there:

                    one shape                           the other
  the system prompt a message with role=system          a top-level argument
  tool schemas      nested under "function"             flat, with input_schema
  tool results      a message with role=tool            a content block on a user turn
  the reply body    message.content, a string           a list of typed blocks
  token usage       prompt_tokens / completion_tokens   input_tokens / output_tokens
  the stop reason   "stop" / "length" / "tool_calls"    "end_turn" / "max_tokens" / "tool_use"

  (the stand-in received the system prompt as: You are an analyst for M…)

Six translations, and not one of them is exotic. That is the argument for the
gateway: none of these differences is hard, and all of them are load-bearing,
so the cost of not having one place to put them is that all six leak into
application code and stay there.

The stop reason is the one worth dwelling on. Both providers can tell you an
answer was cut off, and they use different words for it, and almost every
codebase that has not thought about this ignores the field entirely — which
means a truncated answer is indistinguishable from a finished one all the way
up to the user.

Note what the interface does *not* expose: streaming granularity, provider
error classes, model-specific parameters. Every one of those is a place a
provider leaks through an abstraction that claimed to hide it, and the
discipline is to add them only when a second provider forces you to.

And be honest about what has been tested here. The block-shaped adapter ran
against a stand-in that speaks that wire format, not against a hosted model.
That tests the translation — which is the part that breaks — and it does not
test the model. §27.4 is the part that needs a real account.
